Often as good as the real thing. 😉

Because deterrence doesn’t necessarily require the threat itself. It requires the observer to believe the threat is credible.

A scarecrow doesn’t have to be a farmer. A gargoyle doesn’t have to be a demon.

The representation can produce the same behavioral effect as the reality it represents.

At least until something tests the difference.

And that’s the fascinating part: sometimes a symbol, story, reputation, or illusion can have very real consequences.

The map isn’t the territory. But the map can change how creatures move through the territory.

